# Test/temp data
photos/
@eaDir/

# The Docker config bind mount, which docker-compose.yml puts INSIDE the clone
# and docker-entrypoint.sh seeds on first run. Its scoring_config.json is the
# live config of a running install: viewer.password, users.*.password_hash,
# upload.password, frame.tokens and immich.api_key, all plaintext. The backups
# and the secret beside it were already caught by the basename globs below —
# the live file was the one gap, and it is the one that always exists.
facet-config/

# Deployment knobs — copied from .env.example and then filled in with real
# values (PHOTOS_DIR, DB_PATH, and whatever else a site adds).
.env

# The live config of a native install. It is the operator's OVERRIDE over the
# defaults shipped in config/scoring_config.default.json — per-install by
# definition, rewritten in place by the viewer's own weights, priorities,
# password and share-secret writers, and holding viewer.password,
# users.*.password_hash, upload.password, frame.tokens and immich.api_key in
# plaintext. It was tracked, which is how a developer's local edits became the
# project's shipped config and how that config drifted fourteen keys away from
# the defaults every fresh install actually starts from.
scoring_config.json

# The library lock and the cull-preview cache, written beside the database at
# runtime. Never part of a checkout.
.facet_cache/

# Config backups — both the bare name the secret migration and the password
# upgrade write, and the timestamped ones from the config writers. The bare
# name is NOT covered by the `.backup.*` pattern: it has no suffix.
scoring_config.json.backup
scoring_config.json.backup.*

# Server secret — signs every session JWT and frame link. Never tracked: it
# used to live in scoring_config.json and got committed from there. The glob
# also covers the `.facet_secret.tmp*` scratch file every owner-only write
# stages through: a crash between the write and the rename leaves that copy
# behind, and under mkstemp's default name it was stageable.
.facet_secret*

# Scratch file every scoring_config.json replacement stages through. It is a
# COMPLETE copy of the config — password hashes included — so a crash between
# the write and the rename must not leave a stageable name behind.
.scoring_config.tmp*

# Claude Code
.claude/todos.md
.claude/snapshot*.txt
.claude/review-all/
.codegraph/

# Build output
dist/

# Node — package.json pins every DIRECT dependency exactly, but that says
# nothing about the transitive graph, which npm re-resolves from the registry
# on every build. The lock file is tracked so it cannot drift.
client/node_modules/

# ML model cache
.fastembed_cache/
model-cache/

# Misc
output.log
